[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113397,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ductal papillomas (DPs) are benign epithelial neoplasms arising from the main excretory salivary ducts.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:13:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113398,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8503/0 Intraductal papilloma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:13:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113399,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E91.Z &amp; XA5T23 &amp; XH4LZ4 Benign neoplasm of major salivary glands, unspecified &amp; Salivary gland apparatus &amp; Intraductal papilloma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:13:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113400,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> intraductal papilloma; inverted ductal papilloma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:13:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113401,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:13:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113402,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Preferential sites are intraoral minor salivary glands, with the lower lip, buccal mucosa, and palate being the most frequent {11458248; 33526223; 31209701}. Rare DPs affect the parotid or unusual sites {32744904; 29768362}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:13:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113403,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "<p>DPs present as slowly growing, painless submucosal lesions or as polypoid intraoral lesions. The duration of symptoms ranges from a few weeks to several years {11458248; 26583524}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-12T10:48:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113404,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DPs constitute about 0.3% of oral salivary gland tumours {33526223}. They usually affect adults, with no sex predilection {11555769; 12121243; 17598121}. Rare paediatric cases have been reported {11458248; 33526223; 31209701}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:13:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113405,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "<p >A relationship with trauma has been reported {24455058}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T12:26:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113406,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "<p >HPV DNA was detected in only 1&nbsp;case {18774261; 28329525}. No genetic changes were identified {31505033}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T12:26:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113407,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "<p >DPs appear as cystic nodules measuring &lt;&nbsp;15&nbsp;mm {11458248}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T12:26:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113408,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DP may be described as intraductal papilloma or inverted ductal papilloma, according to the growth pattern {11458248; 31209701; 33526223}. Intraductal papillomas are usually located at the ostia of the salivary excretory ducts, presenting as a unicystic lesion with well-defined borders and filled with papillary projections. Papillae are lined by columnar cells intermingled with rare mucoid cells. Inverted ductal papilloma is an unencapsulated, endophytic epithelial tumour with well-defined borders and a central opening that is frequently in contact with the surface mucosa. It is composed of mucinous and non-keratinizing squamous cells. No atypia is seen, and mitoses are rare {11555769; 12121243; 17598121}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry is of little help in the diagnosis.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The entities include other salivary gland papillary lesions {33526223} such as mucinous adenocarcinoma {29738361} and mucoepidermoid carcinoma. The presence of branching papillae lined by numerous pale, gastric-like cells favours mucinous adenocarcinoma. Atypia, invasive borders, and the presence of <em>MAML2</em> fusion favour the diagnosis of mucoepidermoid carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:13:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113409,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Rarely reported cases show smears with papillary tissue fragments and sheets of ductal or oncocytic columnar cells with bland nuclei, and histiocytes in the background {10349381; 10578993}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:13:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113410,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:13:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113411,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "<h5>Intraductal papilloma</h5>\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a unicystic lesion with internal papillae, lined by columnar cells lacking atypia.</p>\r\n<h5>Inverted ductal papilloma</h5>\r\n<p><em>Essential: </em>well-delineated borders and endophytic growth, composed of squamous and mucoid cells devoid of atypia.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T12:27:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113412,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:13:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113413,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 71,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DPs are benign, cured by complete surgical excision {11458248}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:13:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]